<title>DUBAI: ADNOC lifts August crude prices 85-90 cents.</title>
<headline>ADNOC lifts August crude prices 85-90 cents.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Abu Dhabi National Oil Company said it had increased the price of its crude lifted in August by 85-90 cents a barrel.</p>
<p>Murban is increased 90 cents to $20.45, Lower Zakum is up 85 cents at $20.50, Umm Shaif is increased 90 cents to $20.15 and Upper Zakum rose by 90 cents to $18.75.</p>
</text>
